      "functionality": "Accepts 128-bit inbound packets carrying validated model responses or control/ack packets, performs depacketization and packet validity checks, maintains request sequencing and response age tracking, applies timeout and stale-data rejection, clamps and optionally rate-limits the accepted actuator recommendation, and exposes a deterministic safe fallback actuator command when the external service is unavailable, stale, duplicate, out-of-order, or otherwise invalid. Generates 128-bit outbound request packets from configuration state, latest accepted control inputs, and current request sequence counter, with proper valid/ready backpressure. Provides a compact register window for programming enable, fallback command, clamp limits, rate limit, timeout threshold, stale threshold, debug counters, and latched status/fault indicators.",
      "responsibilities": [
        "Own the top-level packet transport interfaces for outbound request and inbound response streams.",
        "Maintain a monotonically increasing request sequence counter and last accepted response sequence.",
        "Pack request descriptors from configuration registers and latest control inputs into 128-bit outbound packets.",
        "Unpack inbound response packets and extract candidate actuator command, sequence, age, flags, and handle metadata.",
        "Reject duplicate, out-of-order, stale, malformed, or timed-out responses.",
        "Apply clamp limits and optional rate limiting before committing actuator output.",
        "Drive deterministic safe fallback actuator command on reset, timeout, stale data, invalid packet, or fault conditions.",
        "Expose latched status flags and counters through the register window.",
        "Use only compact scalar actuator outputs; no tensor, mesh, or large payload ports are exposed."
      ],
